findings.description:
`FixedPrecisionTensor.reconstruct` overwrites `self.child` in place, so after one call the caller's shared tensor no longer holds its RST shares. It also isn't used by `TorchTensor.reconstruct`, which goes through `self.child.get()` → `AbstractTensor.get` and returns a new tensor. Make this return a new tensor too, for example by delegating to `self.get()`.

```suggestion
    def reconstruct(self):
        if not isinstance(self.child, ReplicatedSharingTensor):
            raise ValueError("reconstruct can only be called on RST")
        return self.get()
```
